{
  "date": "2026-10-20",
  "base_revision": "95a2a7c",
  "kernel": "7.0.0-38-generic",
  "environment": "Patched QEMU 11.1.2, KVM, one host-model vCPU, 1 GiB RAM; physical FL2000 USB port hostbus=2 hostport=2; 64 MiB host USBFS allowance. Modules loaded only in guests.",
  "production_source_changed": false,
  "queue_depth": 3,
  "display_limit": "Attached sink advertises only 800x480 at 66 Hz; 1080p60 timings are synthetic and establish no visible-image result.",
  "method": [
    "Request 60 full-frame DIRTYFB updates/s; record successful whole-frame USB completions with usbmon and trim two seconds at each end of the longest matching-frame-size run.",
    "RGB888 and XRGB8888 use 6,220,800-byte RGB888 wire frames; RGB565 uses 4,147,200-byte frames. Rates use decimal MB/s.",
    "Function profiling and USB tracing enabled; results are transport diagnostics, not clean CPU benchmarks.",
    "Status sampling uses a separate current-source test module with periodic work through the existing interrupt worker; no competing destructive status reader. The sampling patch is not a production change.",
    "A host-only libusb interposer rejects the third 6,220,800-byte OUT submission once with LIBUSB_ERROR_NO_MEM; its subsequent submissions call real libusb.",
    "Expected ENOENT/ESHUTDOWN during modeset/unload and ENODEV after QMP removal are not classified as kernel faults.",
    "The earliest prototype and pre-format builds are recorded explicitly; final builds narrow retry fallback to OUT and differ only in formatting thereafter."
  ],
  "patch_sha256": "5d5f0c1104833932d9492cb04750c9ad0a147f7c69aaa0f1fb2c8a229aed9909",
